job: size final_name to ctx->cache in cache_write_complete, fixes F-006

From: Andy Green <andy@warmcat.com>

cache_write_complete() copied the cache path up to the '~' temp marker
into final_name[128], but vhost cache bases up to JG2_CACHE_BASE_MAX
(256) chars are explicitly supported, producing final names of ~287
bytes... a 159-byte stack smash on the first cache finalize for any
base over 91 chars.  Size the buffer to ctx->cache like the sibling
ctx->cache[384] so every accepted base fits.
---
 lib/job/job.c |    9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/lib/job/job.c b/lib/job/job.c
index 9524a2c..86721b3 100644
--- a/lib/job/job.c
+++ b/lib/job/job.c
@@ -482,7 +482,14 @@ timeval_us(struct timeval *t)
 static void
 cache_write_complete(struct jg2_ctx *ctx)
 {
-	char final_name[128], *p;
+	/*
+	 * The final name is ctx->cache up to the '~'... cache bases up to
+	 * JG2_CACHE_BASE_MAX (256) chars are accepted, which with the on-disk
+	 * structure overhead gives final names longer than 128 bytes.  Size
+	 * the buffer for the whole cache path so accepted bases cannot
+	 * overflow it.
+	 */
+	char final_name[sizeof(ctx->cache)], *p;
 
 	close(ctx->fd_cache);
 	ctx->fd_cache = -1;
